JPEG encoder and decoder: libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0
================================

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

Official source: https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/releases/tag/3.2.0
Pinned source hashes, file selection and tool versions: sources/jpeg/sources.lock.json
Rebuild recipe and our MIT bridge: sources/jpeg/README.md, build.py, bridge.c.

The libjpeg API library uses the IJG License in libjpeg-turbo-README.ijg.
The Modified BSD License and the upstream component overview are preserved in
libjpeg-turbo-LICENSE. Copyright headers from linked source files are retained
in JPEG-RUNTIME-NOTICE, including Thomas G. Lane, Guido Vollbeding, Ken Murchison,
D. R. Commander and other named contributors. Source bytes of the selected
upstream files are unchanged; our separate bridge and adapters are by Ilya Barilo.

This build uses Emscripten 6.0.9, CMake 4.4.3 and Ninja 1.13.2. It links the
libjpeg encoding and decoding API with emmalloc and the Emscripten C runtime. It does not
link TurboJPEG, PNG/libspng, platform assembly SIMD, libc++ or libde265/libheif.
Those HEIC libraries remain separately documented components of the application.

